          "answer": "**This is an emergency. Please contact someone now.** If you might act on these thoughts, or you are in immediate danger, call your local emergency number now. In the United States, you can call or text 988 for the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline. Other countries have equivalent services. The guidance I was given says that thoughts of suicide are a reason to reach a person immediately, not to wait for a routine appointment (red-flag-suicidal-ideation).\n\nThank you for telling me how you are feeling. Feeling hopeless is exhausting, and you do not have to carry it alone.\n\nPlease do these things right now:\n\n- **Move the tablets out of reach.** Take them out of the cupboard and put them somewhere hard to get to, or give them to someone you trust to keep for you. Putting distance between you and them can make a real difference in a hard moment.\n- **Reach a person you trust.** Call or go to someone near you, and tell them what you told me. You can say, \"I am not safe right now and I need you to be with me.\"\n- **Do not stay alone with this.** If you cannot reach anyone, call emergency services or the crisis line listed above.\n\nIf you can, tell me which country you are in, and I can help you find the right number.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
